{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c82d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a087b3-56b9-7060-8f60-96db20969afb"},"sequence":625,"recorded_at":1780531400001245,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"b50cb893-1a9e-463b-98b6-7c1306fa57ef","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"b50cb893-1a9e-463b-98b6-7c1306fa57ef","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"b50cb893-1a9e-463b-98b6-7c1306fa57ef"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a087b4-c3cb-7c82-bef6-4bf30eddb91f"},"task_id":"01a087b4-c3cb-7c82-bef6-4bf30eddb91f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a087b4-c3cb-7c82-bef6-4bf30eddb91f","chunk":"Read text file `internal/sessquery/plan.go`.\n1|// Immutable SelectionPlan construction and current-fact revalidation\n2|// for the v0.6.0 selector contract (SPEC Section 14.7.2).\n3|//\n4|// Resolve the key to a session UUID once per invocation or confirmed\n5|// plan, then bind the selection facts into a machine-local immutable\n6|// plan: the literal selector, the selected session and its validated\n7|// immutable record digest, the selected source (host and exact alias),\n8|// the digests of the complete validated index read and the effective\n9|// validated configuration, the validated winning lease facts, the\n10|// validated authority heads, and the caller-declared action,\n11|// destination, and expectations. No plan hash, name, source, or display\n12|// field is a capability.\n13|//\n14|// Two members of the sixteen-row contract table stay unbound in this\n15|// story boundary, and the plan carries no placeholder for them: there\n16|// are no Lease Record objects in this stack, so lease_record_id has no\n17|// validated digest to bind, and authority heads bind the validated\n18|// event-head digests only. The winning lease triple (epoch, lease ID,\n19|// owner) binds from the validated envelope derivation instead. The\n20|// lease-record runtime owns extending this binding; the plan shape\n21|// documents the exact delta so a future member without a row fails its\n22|// publication gate closed instead of falling into a default.\n23|//\n24|// Revalidation rereads the current configuration and the plan's source,\n25|// validates the same immutable record, the current winning lease, and\n26|// the action prerequisites this leaf can check, and compares every\n27|// bound plan fact in a fixed order. A changed mapping, alias,\n28|// allowlist, transport, source index, record, authority head, lease,\n29|// action, destination, or expectation invalidates the plan with\n30|// selector_plan_stale naming the first diverged member; explicit\n31|// authorization revocation returns peer_not_allowlisted; failed reads\n32|// retain their read-failure classification. Revalidation never\n33|// re-resolves by name, substitutes a same-named session, silently\n34|// replans, transfers a lease, or reuses confirmation for new facts.\n35|//\n36|// Effect authorization beyond read projection — fencing, commit,\n37|// retry, recovery, remote dispatch/admission, and transport-resume\n38|// prerequisites, and the composed per-endpoint invocation bindings —\n39|// belongs to the CLI and lifecycle owners, which invoke Revalidate at\n40|// every boundary in BoundariesFor for their action. A plan built here\n41|// authorizes read projection only.\n42|package sessquery\n43|\n44|import (\n45|\t\"fmt\"\n46|\n47|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n48|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessrepo\"\n49|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/sessstate\"\n50|)\n51|\n52|// SelectorVersion is the exact selector contract version every plan binds.\n53|const SelectorVersion = \"1.0.0\"\n54|\n55|// Plan actions admitted by the Section 14.7.2 boundary matrix. Each is\n56|// an existing command/action tag; binding one selects it, never an\n57|// umbrella bypass.\n58|const (\n59|\tActionStatus      = \"status\"\n60|\tActionAttach      = \"attach\"\n61|\tActionTakeover    = \"takeover\"\n62|\tActionFork        = \"fork\"\n63|\tActionStop        = \"stop\"\n64|\tActionResume      = \"resume\"\n65|\tActionSync        = \"sync\"\n66|\tActionDiff        = \"diff\"\n67|\tActionMaterialize = \"materialize\"\n68|\tActionSetProfile  = \"session.set-profile\"\n69|\tActionLogs        = \"logs\"\n70|\tActionCancel      = \"cancel\"\n71|)\n72|\n73|// Plan boundaries from the normative action/boundary matrix. A boundary\n74|// is reached only when the existing operation reaches that phase; these\n75|// rows introduce no new effects.\n76|const (\n77|\tBoundaryProjection      = \"projection\"\n78|\tBoundaryPreEffect       = \"pre-effect\"\n79|\tBoundaryFencing         = \"fencing\"\n80|\tBoundaryCommit          = \"commit\"\n81|\tBoundaryRetry           = \"retry\"\n82|\tBoundaryRecovery        = \"recovery\"\n83|\tBoundaryRemoteDispatch  = \"remote-dispatch\"\n84|\tBoundaryRemoteAdmission = \"remote-admission\"\n85|\tBoundaryTransportResume = \"transport-resume\"\n86|)\n87|\n88|// planBoundaries is the closed action/boundary matrix: every action has\n89|// exactly its normative row, and an unknown action has none.\n90|var planBoundaries = map[string][]string{\n91|\tActionStatus:      {BoundaryProjection, BoundaryRetry},\n92|\tActionAttach:      {BoundaryPreEffect, BoundaryFencing, BoundaryRetry, BoundaryRemoteDispatch, BoundaryRemoteAdmission, BoundaryTransportResume},\n93|\tActionTakeover:    {BoundaryPreEffect, BoundaryFencing, BoundaryCommit, BoundaryRetry, BoundaryRecovery, BoundaryTransportResume},\n94|\tActionFork:        {BoundaryPreEffect, BoundaryFencing, BoundaryCommit, BoundaryRetry, BoundaryRecovery, BoundaryTransportResume},\n95|\tActionStop:        {BoundaryPreEffect, BoundaryFencing, BoundaryCommit, BoundaryRetry, BoundaryRecovery, BoundaryTransportResume},\n96|\tActionResume:      {BoundaryPreEffect, BoundaryFencing, BoundaryCommit, BoundaryRetry, BoundaryRecovery, BoundaryTransportResume},\n97|\tActionSync:        {BoundaryPreEffect, BoundaryFencing, BoundaryCommit, BoundaryRetry, BoundaryRecovery, BoundaryTransportResume},\n98|\tActionDiff:        {BoundaryProjection, BoundaryRetry},\n99|\tActionMaterialize: {BoundaryPreEffect, BoundaryFencing, BoundaryCommit, BoundaryRetry, BoundaryRecovery},\n100|\tActionSetProfile:  {BoundaryPreEffect, BoundaryFencing, BoundaryCommit, BoundaryRetry, BoundaryRecovery},\n101|\tActionLogs:        {BoundaryProjection, BoundaryRetry, BoundaryRemoteDispatch, BoundaryRemoteAdmission, BoundaryTransportResume},\n102|\tActionCancel:      {BoundaryProjection},\n103|}\n104|\n105|// BoundariesFor returns the required boundary classes for a plan\n106|// action. The boolean reports whether the action is a known tag; an\n107|// unknown action binds no boundary and builds no plan.\n108|func BoundariesFor(action string) ([]string, bool) {\n109|\tboundaries, ok := planBoundaries[action]\n110|\tif !ok {\n111|\t\treturn nil, false\n112|\t}\n113|\treturn append([]string(nil), boundaries...), true\n114|}\n115|\n116|// SelectionPlan is the machine-local immutable binding of one selector\n117|// resolution. All members are values, never references: there is no\n118|// mutator, and Marshal carries the locally verified canonical digest\n119|// so a persisted plan is tamper-evident. Caller-supplied digest\n120|// equality alone is never evidence of authority; only Revalidate\n121|// against current facts decides currency.\n122|type SelectionPlan struct {\n123|\t// SelectorVersion is exactly SelectorVersion.\n124|\tSelectorVersion string\n125|\t// Selector is the original single argument, at most\n126|\t// MaxSelectorRunes characters.\n127|\tSelector string\n128|\t// SessionID is the selected UUIDv7, never resolved again by name.\n129|\tSessionID string\n130|\t// SessionRecordID is the validated immutable Session Record digest.\n131|\tSessionRecordID string\n132|\t// SourceHostID is the UUIDv7 of the selected source, or empty\n133|\t// while the local host identity stays unknown.\n134|\tSourceHostID string\n135|\t// SourceAlias is the exact configured alias, or nil for local. It\n136|\t// is a diagnostic label, never identity.\n137|\tSourceAlias *string\n138|\t// SourceIndexDigest is the digest of the complete validated index\n139|\t// read used for selection.\n140|\tSourceIndexDigest string\n141|\t// ConfigurationDigest is the digest of the effective validated\n142|\t// configuration, including peer mapping, allowlist, and transport.\n143|\tConfigurationDigest string\n144|\t// LeaseEpoch, LeaseID, and OwnerHostID come from the validated\n145|\t// winning envelope lease: positive uint53, UUIDv4, and UUIDv7. All\n146|\t// three stay empty together while no winning lease is observed;\n147|\t// unknown is unknown, never a placeholder.\n148|\tLeaseEpoch  uint64\n149|\tLeaseID     string\n150|\tOwnerHostID string\n151|\t// AuthorityHeads is the sorted unique digest array of the\n152|\t// validated event heads used for the decision: the tail event\n153|\t// digest of the selected validated chain.\n154|\tAuthorityHeads []string\n155|\t// Action is the explicit command/action tag bound at build time.\n156|\tAction string\n157|\t// DestinationHostID is the explicit destination UUIDv7, or nil\n158|\t// when the action takes no destination.\n159|\tDestinationHostID *string\n160|\t// ExpectationDigest binds the caller-declared action expectations\n161|\t// (canonically encoded JSON) for change detection. It does not\n162|\t// replace the checkpoint, workspace, cohort, provider, terminal,\n163|\t// or confirmation contracts, which have no owners in this leaf.\n164|\tExpectationDigest string\n165|}\n166|\n167|// PlanArgs declares the invocation facts BuildPlan binds: the literal\n168|// selector, the explicit action tag, the explicit destination (empty\n169|// for none), and the opaque caller expectations (nil for none).\n170|type PlanArgs struct {\n171|\tSelector     string\n172|\tAction       string\n173|\tDestination  string\n174|\tExpectations []byte\n175|}\n176|\n177|// BuildPlan resolves the selector once through the shared path and\n178|// binds the current facts into an immutable plan. The destination is\n179|// independently validated as a UUIDv7; expectations must be canonically\n180|// encodable JSON and bind by digest for change detection only.\n181|func (reader *Reader) BuildPlan(args PlanArgs) (SelectionPlan, error) {\n182|\tparsed, err := ParseSelector(args.Selector)\n183|\tif err != nil {\n184|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n185|\t}\n186|\tif reader == nil || reader.Local == nil {\n187|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: local repository is required\", ErrUnavailable)\n188|\t}\n189|\tconfig, err := reader.validatedConfiguration()\n190|\tif err != nil {\n191|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n192|\t}\n193|\tif _, ok := BoundariesFor(args.Action); !ok {\n194|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: unknown plan action %q\", ErrInvalidArgument, args.Action)\n195|\t}\n196|\tvar destination *string\n197|\tif args.Destination != \"\" {\n198|\t\tid, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(args.Destination)\n199|\t\tif err != nil {\n200|\t\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: malformed destination host ID: %v\", ErrInvalidArgument, err)\n201|\t\t}\n202|\t\tvalue := id.String()\n203|\t\tdestination = &value\n204|\t}\n205|\texpectations, err := fingerprintExpectations(args.Expectations)\n206|\tif err != nil {\n207|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n208|\t}\n209|\tvar selected Selection\n210|\tif parsed.Source != SourceBare {\n211|\t\tselected, err = reader.resolveExplicit(parsed, config)\n212|\t} else {\n213|\t\tselected, err = reader.resolveBare(parsed, config)\n214|\t}\n215|\tif err != nil {\n216|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n217|\t}\n218|\treturn reader.bindPlan(parsed, config, selected, args.Action, destination, expectations)\n219|}\n220|\n221|// bindPlan reads the winning source completely and binds every plan\n222|// member from validated current facts. The session is located by its\n223|// UUID in the winning source only, never re-resolved by name.\n224|func (reader *Reader) bindPlan(parsed Selector, config validatedConfig, selected Selection, action string, destination *string, expectations string) (SelectionPlan, error) {\n225|\trows, err := reader.readSource(selected.repo, selected.PeerHostID)\n226|\tif err != nil {\n227|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n228|\t}\n229|\tindex, err := fingerprintIndex(reader, selected.repo, rows, selected.PeerHostID)\n230|\tif err != nil {\n231|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n232|\t}\n233|\tconfiguration, err := fingerprintConfiguration(reader, config)\n234|\tif err != nil {\n235|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n236|\t}\n237|\tvar recordID string\n238|\tfound := false\n239|\tfor _, row := range rows {\n240|\t\tif row.Projection.SessionID == selected.SessionID {\n241|\t\t\trecordID, found = row.Projection.RecordID, true\n242|\t\t\tbreak\n243|\t\t}\n244|\t}\n245|\tif !found {\n246|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: selection absent from source index\", ErrPlanStale)\n247|\t}\n248|\tprojection, err := (&sessstate.Projector{Repo: selected.repo, LocalHostID: reader.LocalHostID}).Project(selected.SessionID)\n249|\tif err != nil {\n250|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n251|\t}\n252|\ttail, err := chainTail(selected.repo, selected.SessionID)\n253|\tif err != nil {\n254|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n255|\t}\n256|\tplan := SelectionPlan{\n257|\t\tSelectorVersion:     SelectorVersion,\n258|\t\tSelector:            parsed.Raw,\n259|\t\tSessionID:           selected.SessionID,\n260|\t\tSessionRecordID:     recordID,\n261|\t\tSourceIndexDigest:   index,\n262|\t\tConfigurationDigest: configuration,\n263|\t\tLeaseEpoch:          projection.Winner.Epoch,\n264|\t\tLeaseID:             projection.Winner.LeaseID,\n265|\t\tOwnerHostID:         projection.OwnerHostID,\n266|\t\tAction:              action,\n267|\t\tDestinationHostID:   destination,\n268|\t\tExpectationDigest:   expectations,\n269|\t}\n270|\tif selected.PeerHostID == \"\" {\n271|\t\tif config.localHost != \"\" {\n272|\t\t\tplan.SourceHostID = config.localHost\n273|\t\t}\n274|\t} else {\n275|\t\tplan.SourceHostID = selected.PeerHostID\n276|\t\t// Null marks the local source only. An alias-less peer binds\n277|\t\t// empty: the host still distinguishes it from local.\n278|\t\talias := config.aliasFor(selected.PeerHostID)\n279|\t\taliasCopy := alias\n280|\t\tplan.SourceAlias = &aliasCopy\n281|\t}\n282|\tif tail != \"\" {\n283|\t\tplan.AuthorityHeads = []string{tail}\n284|\t} else {\n285|\t\tplan.AuthorityHeads = []string{}\n286|\t}\n287|\tif err := checkPlanShapes(plan); err != nil {\n288|\t\treturn SelectionPlan{}, err\n289|\t}\n290|\treturn plan, nil\n291|}\n292|\n293|// chainTail returns the tail event digest of a validated session chain,\n294|// or empty when the chain carries no events yet.\n295|func chainTail(repo *sessrepo.Repository, sessionID string) (string, error) {\n296|\tevents, err := repo.ListEvents(sessionID)\n297|\tif err != nil {\n298|\t\treturn \"\", err\n299|\t}\n300|\tif len(events) == 0 {\n301|\t\treturn \"\", nil\n302|\t}\n303|\treturn events[len(events)-1].EventID, nil\n304|}","final_result":true}}}
